## Visual transcription of the SoO (Emergency Exhaust)

### GENERAL:

1. THE EMERGENCY EXHAUST SYSTEM SHALL BE CONTROLLED BY A DEDICATED CONTROLLER AND NETWORKED TO THE BAS.
2. ALL PROGRAMMING SHALL RESIDE LOCAL TO THE CONTROLLER AND UNITS SHALL CONTINUE TO OPERATE UPON A LOSS OF NETWORK COMMUNICATIONS.
3. ALL SETPOINTS SHALL BE ADJUSTABLE.

### LEAD / STANDBY OPERATION:

1. THE EMERGENCY EXHAUST SYSTEM CONSISTS OF PARALLEL FANS IN AN N+1, LEAD / STANDBY CONFIGURATION, ONE FAN SHALL OPERATE AT A TIME
2. THE LEAD UNIT ASSIGNMENT SHALL BE ROTATED WEEKLY.
3. UPON FAILURE OF THE LEAD FAN, THE STANDBY FAN SHALL AUTOMATICALLY START AND AN ALARM SHALL BE INDICATED.

### FAN AND DAMPER CONTROL:

1. UPON A SIGNAL FROM THE TOXIC GAS MONITORING SYSTEM OR THE EMERGENCY ACTIVATION SWITCH, THE OUTSIDE AIR ISOLATION DAMPER SHALL OPEN AND BE PROVEN OPEN VIA A DAMPER END SWITCH.
2. THE EXHAUST ISOLATION DAMPER ON THE ALARMING ROOM SHALL OPEN, AND BE PROVEN OPEN VIA AN END SWITCH.
3. THE LEAD FANS ISOLATION DAMPER SHALL OPEN.
4. THE LEAD FAN SHALL BE ENERGIZED.
5. THE BYPASS SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN THE MINIMUM STACK OUTLET VELOCITY.
6. THE FAN SHALL CONTINUE TO OPERATE UNTIL THE TGMS INDICATES NORMAL LEVELS FOR MORE THAN 15 MINUTES OR THE SYSTEM IS MANUALLY RESET.

### OUTDOOR AIR TEMPERATURE CONTROL:

1. THE OUTSIDE AIR SHALL BE TEMPERED BY THE ELECTRIC HEATING COIL.
2. FLOW SHALL BE PROVEN VIA THE AIRFLOW SWITCH.
3. THE ELECTRIC COIL SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN 68 DEG F DISHARGE AIR TEMP.

### SYSTEM TEST:

1. A WEEKLY TEST SHALL BE PERFORMED TO VERIFY FUNCTIONALITY OF THE SYSTEM. COORDINATE WITH OWNER FOR TEST SCHEDULE TIMING.
2. UPON INITIATING THE TEST THE FOLLOWING SHALL OCCUR:
   A. THE FAN SET’S BYPASS DAMPER SHALL BE STROKED FULLY OPEN AND CLOSED AGAIN AND PROVEN VIA THE END SWITCH
   B. CHASE 1 EXHAUST ISOLATION DAMPER SHALL OPEN AND PROVE OPEN VIA THE END SWITCH.
   C. FAN EF-1A DAMPER SHALL OPEN AND PROVE OPEN VIA THE END SWITCH.
   D. FAN EF-1A SHALL START AND OPERATE AT ITS LOWEST SPEED, WITH THE BYPASS DAMPER MODULATING TO MAINTAIN STACK VELOCITY.
   E. CHASE 1 SUPPLY ISOLATION DAMPER SHALL OPEN AND PROVE OPEN VIA THE END SWITCH.
   F. SUPPLY FAN SF-1 SHALL START AND PROVE ON VIA THE CT.
   G. EHC-1 SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN 60 DEGREES F DAT.
   H. THE TEST SHALL CONTINUE FOR 3 MINUTES AFTER WHICH THE TEST SHALL SWITCH TO EXHAUST FAN EF-1B AND CHASE 2 TO PERFORM THE SAME TEST FOR AN ADDITIONAL 3 MINUTES.
   I. ANY FAILURES OF DAMPERS OR FANS SHALL GENERATE AN ALARM IN THE BAS.
   J. TEST RESULTS SHALL BE LOGGED AND TRENDED IN THE BAS.

